<h2 id="benefits-of-virtual-generated-columns" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Benefits of Virtual Generated Columns</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#benefits-of-virtual-generated-columns" aria-label="Link to Benefits of Virtual Generated Columns"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>Now that we understand the basics, let&#x27;s explore the benefits of using virtual generated columns in PostgreSQL 18.</p>
<h3 id="storage-space-savings" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Storage Space Savings</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#storage-space-savings" aria-label="Link to Storage Space Savings"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>Virtual columns consume no disk storage, leading to significant space savings, especially for large datasets with complex calculations. This is particularly useful in scenarios where calculated values are not frequently queried or indexed.</p>
<p>To see the storage impact, let&#x27;s add some virtual columns to our <code>products</code> table:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="sql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)">-- Add multiple virtual calculations without storage overhead</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">ALTER</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> TABLE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> products</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="3"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">ADD</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> COLUMN shipping_weight_lbs </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">DECIMAL</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-constant)">6</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">,</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-constant)">2</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">)</span></span>
